      "answer": "Staff may return to work 5 days after symptom onset if they have been fever-free for at least 24 hours without fever-reducing medication and their symptoms are improving, and they must wear a well-fitting mask in all patient care areas through day 10. Staff who work with severely immunocompromised patients should have a negative test on day 5 or later before returning, or remain off work until day 10. This 5-day minimum replaces the 10-day period in the 2019 edition.",
